  "name": "Tangos and tientos (flamenco four-beat palos)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Tangos flamencos are the festive four-beat palo of flamenco, with local schools in Cádiz, Triana, Jerez, Granada and Málaga; La Niña de los Peines made influential 78-rpm recordings of them. Tientos are the slow, heavy form of the same compás, which tradition credits to the Cádiz singer Enrique el Mellizo, and are often sung as an opening that speeds up into tangos.",
  "recipe": "classic Iberian early-1950s tangos and tientos, ballad Poetry, Mediterranean ballad branch, iberian functional song. solo with instrumental accompaniment. cypress body percussive attack strong flamenco tradition rasgueado strum picado scale runs flamenco guitar, hand clap. andalusian tablao seville madrid. Neumann U47, tube pre, colored vintage console, LA-2A optical, passive program EQ. tape 15ips plate reverb.",
